Chapter: CharCodeAtHigh
  cites Foreword chapter Console

Section: Body

 `char-code-at` answers the unsigned byte on every lane. A CCE unit at or above
 code point 128 is made only of bytes at or above 128, so a lane that loads the
 byte signed answers negatives here (plugs-backlog 2.80).

  bytes-of : Text, Integer -> Text
  bytes-of (t) (i) =
    if i >= text-length t then ""
    else " " & show (char-code-at t i) & bytes-of t (i + 1)

  line-for : Integer -> Text
  line-for (cp) = show cp & ":" & bytes-of (char-encode (code-to-char cp)) 0

  opening : [Console] Nothing = act
    print-line-uni (line-for 127)
    print-line-uni (line-for 128)
    print-line-uni (line-for 2175)
    print-line-uni (line-for 100000)
  end
